---
import Layout from '../layouts/layout.astro';

const zones = [
  { n: 1, name: 'Front yard', kind: 'Pop-up sprinklers', minutes: 15, cap: 'no hosing out the front, so summer coverage comes from 3 days a week, not longer runs; heatwave week with the lemon wilting = 20 min for that week, then back to 15', covers: 'Everything out the front: banksia, wattle, westringia, cushion bush, dianellas, gymea, chalk sticks, cotyledon, lemon, feijoa, miscanthus, front kangaroo paws, all three fence muehlenbeckias' },
  { n: 2, name: 'Lawn', kind: 'Pop-up sprinklers plus a drip line', minutes: 12, cap: 'never more than 15, this is the zone that flooded', covers: 'The buffalo lawn, plus the frangipani, its lily turf and the bartlettina living off overspray. Also a drip line with shrubblers (found buried 17 Sept): the composted bed nearest the house (echinacea Sombrero, achillea), the lime, and the sage and strawberry area. A 12 min run is about 5L per shrubbler, so those get the hose on hot days' },
  { n: 3, name: 'Flower beds', kind: 'Drip with bubblers', minutes: 30, cap: 'echinacea and the cutting bed rot if wetter', covers: 'The achillea\'s original bed, black eyed susan, Caradonna, the cutting bed' },
  { n: 4, name: 'Everything out the back', kind: 'Drip', minutes: 60, cap: '', covers: 'All three star jasmine runs (about 20 plants), grapefruit, orange, olive, passionfruit, giant taro, blue star fern, Mexican sage, lavender, dusty miller, rosemary, strawberry, back kangaroo paws' },
];

const frequency = [
  { when: 'September', days: '1 day a week' },
  { when: 'October', days: '2 days a week, three or four apart' },
  { when: 'First 30° day in the forecast', days: '3 days a week' },
  { when: 'April', days: 'back to 1 day a week' },
  { when: 'May', days: 'off at the tap and the controller' },
];

const spares = [
  'Goof plugs (Holman 4mm micro repair plugs) for torn holes',
  '4mm off-take barbs, the joint that goes into the thick pipe',
  '4mm barbed joiners for splicing tube',
  'Pope 300mm riser stakes, the tube clips into the side, the head sits at the top',
  '13mm and 19mm end plugs',
  'Drip punch, use the 4mm side',
  'Still to get: Holman PC Barbed Emitter 10-pack (the shrubbler) and 4mm x 10m flex tube. Both were missing from the September delivery',
];

const replaceSteps = [
  'Zone off. Twist and pull the old body off the 4mm tube. Cut the tube behind it only if it will not budge.',
  'Dip the tube end in a mug of hot water for 10 seconds.',
  'Push the new shrubbler on until the barb is fully in.',
  'Spike a riser stake beside the plant, snap the tube into the clip so the head sits at the top pointing down.',
  'If the old one was pushed straight into the thick pipe and the hole is torn: goof plug it, punch a fresh hole 2cm along, off-take barb in, short tube, shrubbler, stake.',
  'Zone on. A slow steady bubble is right. Read the programme back before closing the lid.',
];

const deadBranches = [
  { see: 'Water squirts from the tube', means: 'The head was blocked.', fix: 'Push a new shrubbler on. Done.' },
  { see: 'Nothing from the tube', means: 'The blockage is further back.', fix: 'Follow the tube back to the thick pipe and pull it off the barb there.' },
  { see: 'Water at the barb', means: 'The tube is kinked or blocked.', fix: 'Cut a fresh length of 4mm tube, hot water both ends, barb one end, shrubbler the other.' },
  { see: 'Nothing at the barb either', means: 'The barb is blocked, or this head is on a different zone.', fix: 'Run the other zones one at a time first (the September \'dead\' bubbler was on zone 2, not 3). Then pull the barb and poke it clear with a pin, or push in a new one.' },
];
---

<Layout title="Irrigation — Garden">
  <div class="animate-in">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <p class="font-medium text-terra uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-1">Quick reference</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold mb-3">Irrigation</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-2xl">
        The four zones and their run times for the controller, then how to fix a dripper, with what is in the shed. Read the
        watering days back before you close the controller lid.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Zones and run times</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {zones.map((z) => (
          <div class="bg-paper rounded-xl border border-rule p-5 flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Zone {z.n} · {z.name}</h3>
              <span class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-terra whitespace-nowrap">{z.minutes} min</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-olive mb-2">{z.kind}{z.cap && <span class="text-ink-faint font-normal"> · {z.cap}</span>}</p>
            <p class="text-ink-soft text-sm">{z.covers}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-5 bg-paper rounded-xl border border-rule p-5">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint mb-2">How often. Run times never change, only the days.</p>
        <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-1.5">
          {frequency.map((f) => (
            <li class="flex gap-2.5 items-baseline">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-terra shrink-0 translate-y-[-2px]"></span>
              <span><strong class="font-semibold">{f.when}</strong> <span class="text-ink-soft">— {f.days}</span></span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-rule-light">
          One start time only, 5 to 6am. Skip a run after a 20mm+ week. Anything out the back that
          wants more than its zone gives it on a hot day is a hose job, never a longer run. The front is
          never hosed: zone 1 has to carry it, so the summer step-up to 3 days a week is what feeds the lemon and feijoa.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-1">Fixing a dripper</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-soft mb-5 max-w-2xl">
        The September 2026 audit repairs are done (17 Sept): every zone runs and every head has been
        checked. This is the reference for next time. Same skill as the May install: pull the old
        part off, push the new one on. Bring garden scissors, a mug of hot water and a pin.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-5">
        <div class="bg-paper rounded-xl border border-rule p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Spares in the shed</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            {spares.map((s) => (
              <li class="flex gap-2.5 items-baseline text-sm">
                <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-terra shrink-0 translate-y-[-2px]"></span>
                <span>{s}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-paper rounded-xl border border-rule p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Before you start</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft text-sm">
            At the controller turn the dial to Manual and start the zone you are working on. You need it
            running to see what is coming out where. A head that stays dry on one zone may belong to
            another, so run each zone in turn before calling anything dead. Turn it off when you are done
            and read the programme back: one start time, the right days.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-paper rounded-xl border border-rule overflow-hidden mb-5">
        <div class="h-1.5 bg-olive"></div>
        <div class="p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Replacing a shrubbler <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint font-sans font-normal">2 min</span></h3>
          <ol class="space-y-1.5 list-decimal pl-6">
            {replaceSteps.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-paper rounded-xl border border-rule overflow-hidden">
        <div class="h-1.5 bg-olive"></div>
        <div class="p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-1">A dead one <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint font-sans font-normal">5 to 10 min</span></h3>
          <p class="font-medium mb-3">Zone running. Pull the head off the tube and look at what comes out.</p>
          <div class="divide-y divide-rule-light border-t border-rule-light">
            {deadBranches.map((b) => (
              <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-x-6 gap-y-1 py-3">
                <p class="font-semibold">{b.see}</p>
                <p><span class="text-ink-soft">{b.means}</span> <span class="font-medium">{b.fix}</span></p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-ink-faint border-t border-rule-light pt-4">
      One rule outranks everything on this page: no bubbler lies under the mulch. Buried ones silt up,
      which is how you ended up fishing for them.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
